Split diagram. Left "SAST": magnifying glass over source-code files, labelled
"reads the code, before running". Right "DAST": OWASP ZAP sending HTTP attack
requests (XSS payload, header checks, injection) at a running web app and reading
responses, labelled "attacks the running app, black box". Center note:
"complementary — run both". Flat style. max-width 860px.
